<title>UK: EU's Legras happy with grain export volume so far.</title>
<headline>EU's Legras happy with grain export volume so far.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>EU farm director-general Guy Legras said on Wednesday he was content with levels of EU grains exports so far this season.</p>
<p>&quot;Until now I think the volume is good. It was less last week because I thought the bids were not very good&quot;, he told reporters at a London Agra Europe conference.  </p>
<p>&quot;Exporters have to be aggressive every week,&quot; Legras said in response to questions on the outlook for the next tender due on Thursday.</p>
<p>He insisted that the level awarded would depend on the world market price and the value of the dollar. &quot;If the dollar goes up, the refund goes down,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Legras declined to be drawn on the level of refund or volume of award he was trying to achieve. &quot;I have to keep them guessing. If they don't I will be squeezed,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom  +171 44 542 7729</p>
